\f0\fs24 \cf0 # Chapter 4 \'97 Locator Strategy\
\
> **Goal:** Build resilient, readable, maintainable, and accessibility-friendly locators by following Playwright's recommended practices.\
\
---\
\
# Overview\
\
A locator is one of the most important parts of an automation framework.\
\
Poor locator strategies are the primary cause of:\
\
- Flaky tests\
- High maintenance costs\
- False failures\
- Slow debugging\
- Fragile automation\
\
A good locator should identify elements the same way a real user does.\
\
Playwright is designed around this philosophy.\
\
**Reference**\
\
https://playwright.dev/docs/locators\
\
---\
\
# Locator Priority\
\
Always choose the highest priority locator available.\
\
| Priority | Locator | Recommended |\
|-----------|----------|-------------|\
| 1 | getByRole() | \uc0\u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088  |\
| 2 | getByLabel() | \uc0\u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088  |\
| 3 | getByPlaceholder() | \uc0\u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088  |\
| 4 | getByText() | \uc0\u11088 \u11088 \u11088  |\
| 5 | getByTestId() | \uc0\u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088 \u11088  |\
| 6 | locator() | \uc0\u11088 \u11088 \u11088  |\
| 7 | XPath | \uc0\u11088  |\
\
