---\
\
# LOC-001\
\
## Rule\
\
Always prefer user-facing locators.\
\
## Severity\
\
Critical\
\
## Why\
\
Automation should interact with the application exactly like a user.\
\
User-facing locators are:\
\
- More stable\
- Easier to understand\
- Accessibility-friendly\
- Recommended by Playwright\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
await page.getByRole('button', \{\
    name: 'Login'\
\}).click();\
```\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
await page.locator('.btn-primary').click();\
```\
\
## Never\
\
```ts\
await page.locator('/html/body/div/div[2]/button').click();\
```\
\
## AI Rule\
\
Always attempt user-facing locators before CSS selectors.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-002\
\
## Rule\
\
Use getByRole() for interactive elements.\
\
## Applies To\
\
- Button\
- Link\
- Checkbox\
- Radio\
- Menu\
- Tab\
- Switch\
- Dialog\
- Listbox\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
await page.getByRole('button', \{\
    name: 'Save'\
\});\
```\
\
```ts\
await page.getByRole('link', \{\
    name: 'Dashboard'\
\});\
```\
\
```ts\
await page.getByRole('checkbox', \{\
    name: 'Remember me'\
\});\
```\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
page.locator('.btn-save')\
```\
\
## Why\
\
Roles rarely change compared to CSS classes.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-003\
\
## Rule\
\
Use accessible names.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.getByRole(\
    'button',\
    \{\
        name: 'Submit'\
    \}\
)\
```\
\
## Avoid\
\
```ts\
page.getByRole('button')\
```\
\
Multiple buttons may exist.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-004\
\
## Rule\
\
Use getByLabel() for form fields.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
await page.getByLabel(\
    'Email'\
).fill(email);\
```\
\
```ts\
await page.getByLabel(\
    'Password'\
).fill(password);\
```\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
page.locator('#email')\
```\
\
## Why\
\
Labels are intended for users.\
\
IDs often change.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-005\
\
## Rule\
\
Use getByPlaceholder() only when labels do not exist.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.getByPlaceholder(\
    'Search...'\
)\
```\
\
## Avoid\
\
Using placeholder if a proper label already exists.\
\
## Why\
\
Placeholder text changes more frequently than labels.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-006\
\
## Rule\
\
Use getByText() only when text uniquely identifies an element.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.getByText(\
    'No Data Available'\
)\
```\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.getByText(\
    'Terms & Conditions'\
)\
```\
\
## Avoid\
\
```ts\
page.getByText(\
    'OK'\
)\
```\
\
Many dialogs contain "OK".\
\
---\
\
# LOC-007\
\
## Rule\
\
Use getByTestId() for custom components.\
\
## Suitable For\
\
- React Component\
- Vue Component\
- Angular Component\
- Charts\
- Canvas Wrapper\
- Custom Dropdown\
- Virtual List\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.getByTestId(\
    'product-card'\
)\
```\
\
```ts\
page.getByTestId(\
    'shopping-cart'\
)\
```\
\
## Why\
\
Complex UI libraries sometimes cannot expose meaningful accessibility information.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-008\
\
## Rule\
\
Never rely on dynamic CSS classes.\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
page.locator(\
'.css-1ab23'\
)\
```\
\
```ts\
page.locator(\
'.MuiButton-root-123'\
)\
```\
\
## Why\
\
Generated classes may change after every build.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-009\
\
## Rule\
\
Avoid positional selectors.\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
locator(\
'button:nth-child(3)'\
)\
```\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
locator(\
'tr:nth-child(5)'\
)\
```\
\
## Why\
\
UI order changes.\
\
Automation breaks.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-010\
\
## Rule\
\
XPath is the last option.\
\
## Allowed\
\
- Legacy applications\
- SVG edge cases\
- XML-based UI\
- No accessible attributes available\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.locator(\
'//svg//*[name()="path"]'\
)\
```\
\
## Never\
\
```ts\
/html/body/div/div[2]/div[5]/button\
```\
\
Absolute XPath is prohibited.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-011\
\
## Rule\
\
Scope locators whenever possible.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
const dialog = page.getByRole('dialog');\
\
await dialog\
    .getByRole('button', \{\
        name: 'Delete'\
    \})\
    .click();\
```\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
page.getByRole(\
    'button',\
    \{\
        name: 'Delete'\
    \}\
)\
```\
\
There may be multiple Delete buttons.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-012\
\
## Rule\
\
Prefer chaining over long selectors.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page\
.getByRole('table')\
.getByRole('row')\
.getByRole('button', \{\
    name: 'Edit'\
\});\
```\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
page.locator(\
'table tbody tr td button'\
)\
```\
\
---\
\
# LOC-013\
\
## Rule\
\
Use filter() for repeated elements.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page\
.getByRole('row')\
.filter(\{\
    hasText: 'John Doe'\
\})\
.getByRole('button', \{\
    name: 'Edit'\
\});\
```\
\
## Why\
\
Filtering is clearer than positional indexing.\
\
---\
\
# LOC-014\
\
## Rule\
\
Use has() when selecting parent elements.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page.locator('article')\
.filter(\{\
    has: page.getByText('Playwright')\
\});\
```\
\
---\
\
# LOC-015\
\
## Rule\
\
Use frameLocator() for iframe.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
page\
.frameLocator('#payment-frame')\
.getByRole('button', \{\
    name: 'Pay'\
\});\
```\
\
## Never\
\
Attempt to interact with iframe content without frameLocator().\
\
---\
\
# LOC-016\
\
## Rule\
\
Prefer Locator over ElementHandle.\
\
## Good\
\
```ts\
const button =\
page.getByRole(\
    'button',\
    \{\
        name: 'Save'\
    \}\
);\
\
await button.click();\
```\
\
## Avoid\
\
```ts\
const handle =\
await page.$(\
'.save'\
);\
```\
\
## Why\
\
Locator supports:\
\
- Auto waiting\
- Retry\
- Better stability\
\
---\
\
# LOC-017\
\
## Rule\
\
Never cache locators globally.\
\
## Good\
\
Create locators inside Page Objects.\
\
## Bad\
\
```ts\
export const loginButton =\
page.getByRole(...)\
```\
\
---\
\
# LOC-018\
\
## Rule\
\
Keep locators inside Page Objects or Component Objects.\
\
## Good\
\
```text\
pages/\
\
LoginPage.ts\
\
DashboardPage.ts\
\
components/\
\
Navbar.ts\
\
Sidebar.ts\
\
Modal.ts\
```\
\
## Never\
\
```text\
tests/login.spec.ts\
\
const button =\
page.locator(...)\
```\
\
---\
\
# Common Mistakes\
\
| Mistake | Risk |\
|----------|------|\
| Absolute XPath | Very High |\
| Dynamic CSS Class | High |\
| nth-child | High |\
| Text Locator Everywhere | Medium |\
| Duplicate Locators | High |\
| Locator Inside Test | High |\
| ElementHandle | Medium |\
| Hardcoded CSS | Medium |\
\
---\
\
# AI Coding Rules\
\
- Prefer user-facing locators.\
- Use getByRole() whenever possible.\
- Use getByLabel() for forms.\
- Use getByPlaceholder() only if labels do not exist.\
- Use getByTestId() for complex UI.\
- Avoid CSS selectors unless necessary.\
- Never generate absolute XPath.\
- Never use nth-child.\
- Scope locators.\
- Use filter() instead of positional selectors.\
- Use frameLocator() for iframes.\
- Keep locators inside Page Objects.\
- Never duplicate locators across multiple files.\
\
---\
\
# Enterprise Checklist\
\
- [ ] Uses accessible locators\
- [ ] No absolute XPath\
- [ ] No dynamic CSS classes\
- [ ] No nth-child selectors\
- [ ] Scoped where necessary\
- [ ] Uses frameLocator() for iframes\
- [ ] Uses filter() for repeated elements\
- [ ] Uses has() when selecting parents\
- [ ] Stored inside Page Objects\
- [ ] Readable and maintainable\
\
---\
\
# Summary\
\
The best locator is the one that most closely represents how a user identifies an element.\
\
**Golden Order**\
\
1. getByRole()\
2. getByLabel()\
3. getByPlaceholder()\
4. getByText()\
5. getByTestId()\
6. locator()\
7. XPath (last resort)\
\
A stable locator strategy significantly reduces flaky tests and long-term maintenance costs.}